      "seed": 352229635,
      "version": 803,
      "versionNonce": 832888109,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1731158178153,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "So in Sql we have Database which carries multiple Table ,In NoSql we have database which have \nmultiple collection //so in nosql collection replaces database\n\nAnd NoSql provide ease of accessing data suppose we want to create a Book collection which store\nbook name,book id ,publish date ,author first name,last name and age \n\nNow if we were developing this in Sql then we would have to maitain a seprate table for author\nwhich will have author id,author first name ,last name and age column then use author id\nas foreign key in Book table\n\n\nlet's see this in action how can we do this :\n ",
      "fontSize": 52.64151862215081,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "So in Sql we have Database which carries multiple Table ,In NoSql we have database which have \nmultiple collection //so in nosql collection replaces database\n\nAnd NoSql provide ease of accessing data suppose we want to create a Book collection which store\nbook name,book id ,publish date ,author first name,last name and age \n\nNow if we were developing this in Sql then we would have to maitain a seprate table for author\nwhich will have author id,author first name ,last name and age column then use author id\nas foreign key in Book table\n\n\nlet's see this in action how can we do this :\n ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "4l3Hq_WS9tSFT0ORi7wDk",
      "type": "image",
      "x": 96.31360235753527,
      "y": 42285.437431801285,
      "width": 1843.9165216214865,
      "height": 1527.7314523026773,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "transparent",
