    {
      "id": "m29Zbp_LsWPaiGW-gXmzu",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -15587.466069077347,
      "y": 243372.48251323725,
      "width": 12697.6650390625,
      "height": 946.1904907226561,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 2,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2S",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1933369005,
      "version": 176,
      "versionNonce": 1024975651,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1731356825297,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Updating Document using MongoDb Shell\n-------------------------------------------------------------",
      "fontSize": 378.47619628906244,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Updating Document using MongoDb Shell\n-------------------------------------------------------------",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "csznNBHjKxRDBCnyEwssc",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -15551.57150931178,
      "y": 244512.7996373592,
      "width": 11140.90234375,
      "height": 14894.471740722654,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 2,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2T",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1289598563,
      "version": 309,
      "versionNonce": 1068135917,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1731357270194,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Let's take a dummy document and try to work on it using update methods:\n\n{\n  \"_id\": ObjectId(\"605c72ef1532073421909b1\"),\n  \"title\": \"Inception\",\n  \"year\": 2010,\n  \"genre\": \"Sci-Fi\",\n  \"rating\": 8.8,\n  \"reviews\": [\n    \"Mind-bending!\",\n    \"Great plot and direction!\",\n    \"Amazing visual effects!\"\n  ],\n  \"cast\": [\n    { \"name\": \"Leonardo DiCaprio\", \"role\": \"Dominick Cobb\" },\n    { \"name\": \"Joseph Gordon-Levitt\", \"role\": \"Arthur\" }\n  ],\n  \"lastModified\": ISODate(\"2024-01-01T00:00:00Z\")\n}\n\nThis is our dummy document let's try to work around it :\n\n\n\nIn MongoDB, when you want to update a document using \nmongosh (Mongo Shell), you use the updateOne() or updateMany() methods for updating documents. \nBelow, I'll show you how to update documents using these commands with various examples.\n\n1. Update One Document\nThe updateOne() method updates only the first document that matches the filter criteria.\n\nSyntax:\ndb.collection.updateOne(\n  <filter>,\n  <update>,\n  <options>\n)\n\nWe have to use $set operator to set the new field value ,\n\ndb.movies.updateOne(\n  { title: \"Inception\" },  // filter\n  { $set: { year: 2011 } }  // update\n);\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n2.Update Multiple Documents\nIf you want to update multiple documents at once, you can use updateMany(). \nThis will update all documents that match the filter criteria.\n\nSyntax:\ndb.collection.updateMany(\n  <filter>,\n  <update>,\n  <options>\n)\nExample:\nLet's say you want to update all movies in the movies collection that have the genre \"Sci-Fi\" and set the year to 2020.\n\ndb.movies.updateMany(\n  { genre: \"Sci-Fi\" },  // filter\n  { $set: { year: 2020 } }  // update\n);\n\n",
      "fontSize": 170.22253417968747,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Let's take a dummy document and try to work on it using update methods:\n\n{\n  \"_id\": ObjectId(\"605c72ef1532073421909b1\"),\n  \"title\": \"Inception\",\n  \"year\": 2010,\n  \"genre\": \"Sci-Fi\",\n  \"rating\": 8.8,\n  \"reviews\": [\n    \"Mind-bending!\",\n    \"Great plot and direction!\",\n    \"Amazing visual effects!\"\n  ],\n  \"cast\": [\n    { \"name\": \"Leonardo DiCaprio\", \"role\": \"Dominick Cobb\" },\n    { \"name\": \"Joseph Gordon-Levitt\", \"role\": \"Arthur\" }\n  ],\n  \"lastModified\": ISODate(\"2024-01-01T00:00:00Z\")\n}\n\nThis is our dummy document let's try to work around it :\n\n\n\nIn MongoDB, when you want to update a document using \nmongosh (Mongo Shell), you use the updateOne() or updateMany() methods for updating documents. \nBelow, I'll show you how to update documents using these commands with various examples.\n\n1. Update One Document\nThe updateOne() method updates only the first document that matches the filter criteria.\n\nSyntax:\ndb.collection.updateOne(\n  <filter>,\n  <update>,\n  <options>\n)\n\nWe have to use $set operator to set the new field value ,\n\ndb.movies.updateOne(\n  { title: \"Inception\" },  // filter\n  { $set: { year: 2011 } }  // update\n);\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n2.Update Multiple Documents\nIf you want to update multiple documents at once, you can use updateMany(). \nThis will update all documents that match the filter criteria.\n\nSyntax:\ndb.collection.updateMany(\n  <filter>,\n  <update>,\n  <options>\n)\nExample:\nLet's say you want to update all movies in the movies collection that have the genre \"Sci-Fi\" and set the year to 2020.\n\ndb.movies.updateMany(\n  { genre: \"Sci-Fi\" },  // filter\n  { $set: { year: 2020 } }  // update\n);\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
